  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: PatClin2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "You have been receiving the standard treatment, but the side effects
    are starting to limit your daily functions. Your doctor discusses a clinical
    trial with you as a potential alternative to the standard treatment, which may
    help with symptom burden. \r\n\n<b>One of the benefits of clinical trials is
    that patients may get access to promising treatments before they\u2019re widely
    available.</b>\n\r\nIs this <b>true</b> or <b>false?</b>"
  explanation: "Clinical trials are the main way new treatments are tested, so participating
    can give patients access to promising new treatments that aren\u2019t yet available
    to the public. While there\u2019s no guarantee the new treatment will work better
    than the standard treatment, trials are designed so patients still receive the
    best-known standard care. This helps protect patients while also advancing research
    for future treatments."
  correctAnswer: True
  incorrectAnswer1: False
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Patient
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: Clinical
